00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.230 align:start position:0%
 
hi there  maybe you can hear in the background  jerry and the pacemakers sing singing  you will never walk alone  which is sort of the the  theme song of the liverpool soccer fans  in england  and i think if we learn languages it's  the same we'll never walk alone  let me just turn him off  but you know it can sometimes seem as if  learning a language is a lonely task you  of course you listen on your own you  read on your own  uh  but there are many ways in which it can  be something that connects you with  other people obviously if you have an  online tutor i just finished having a  conversation with my arabic tutor this  morning  and i spent the weekend  listening doing a lot of listening i  listened five hours on saturday did a  lot of reading and linking and i really  felt  that my  my arabic had improved and i was able to  show that to my tutor  uh  this morning and so i'm connecting i'm  connecting with the content that i  listen to i'm connecting with my tutor  and i know that i'm developing the  ability to connect even more in the  future both with the language and the  culture and with people that i'll be  able to communicate with in the language  and as you learn  there are so many things that you can do  to to sort of  reach out to other members of the  language learning community  uh obviously to connect with the tutor  uh getting getting on our forum  either asking questions or answering  questions about the language you're  learning or your native language  i also think that it's very useful to to  review your statistics maybe in the  community you have the ability to  compare yourself with others  i recently  on one of my language workouts  was asked to review the profile  of several of our members at link and  what was common to all of them was that  they don't listen enough  you should look at what other people are  doing and if you're not listening enough  listen more listen hours and hours get  the language in you it's connecting you  to the language  uh  use your playlists a lot of people don't  use the playlist  save your lessons to a playlist so that  you can carry that with you you're not  walking alone when i walk i listen i'm  connecting to  hopefully content that i find  interesting the content that i'm  listening to now in arabic  even though i don't fully understand it  but after reading it and saving words i  do start to understand it and these are  political podcast discussions with  people their lives and all of this is  enabling me to connect so that i'm not  walking alone  i think part of the the risk let's say  of online language learning is that you  feel that uh you know you're not uh  you know you're not connected how well  am i doing and that's where the  statistics can even if you don't feel  you're improving if you are  you know  totaling up those listening hours those  reading words those links  you are learning and if you can connect  with a tutor so much the better you  don't have to do it every day for hours  even  once a week right now i'm doing  basically two hours a week you're  connecting so it's important  to uh realize that  learning another language is a  tremendously social thing to do  even if you don't have the opportunity  all the time to speak the language  you can listen  uh  you know i mentioned the tutor i get the  tutor's report i can review  uh discussions that i had with my tutor  six months ago again i'm connecting so  language learning is not  even though many of the activities are  solitary activities you have to read on  your own you have to listen on your own  but those are activities that connect  you to people connect you to the  language to native speakers and even to  other learners so i just wanted to make  the point that you're not on your own  we can even put this guy back on  so we don't walk alone  when we learn a language  you're doing something profoundly  social  thank you  and good luck in your ongoing journey

